{"title":"Career Roadmap · Lean Six Sigma Engineer","role":"Lean Six Sigma Engineer","summary":"A Lean Six Sigma Engineer improves manufacturing and business processes by reducing defects, waste, variation, cycle time, downtime, and unnecessary costs. The role combines industrial engineering, statistics, process improvement, quality management, operations research, and data analytics.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Industrial & Production Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Lean Six Sigma Engineer improves manufacturing and business processes by reducing defects, waste, variation, cycle time, downtime, and unnecessary costs. The role combines industrial engineering, statistics, process improvement, quality management, operations research, and data analytics."},{"type":"p","text":"For an Industrial & Production Engineering graduate, this is a highly aligned career pathway. The student should develop strong capabilities in:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Industrial Engineering","Lean Manufacturing","Six Sigma","Statistics","Quality","Operations Research","Data Analytics","Automation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Lean Six Sigma engineers can work in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Automotive"},{"text":"Aerospace"},{"text":"Electronics"},{"text":"Pharmaceuticals"},{"text":"FMCG"},{"text":"Logistics"},{"text":"Healthcare"},{"text":"IT/business-process operations"},{"text":"Consulting"},{"text":"Supply-chain organizations"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus","Typical Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Process Improvement Foundation"},{"text":"Graduate Engineer Trainee → Process Improvement Engineer"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Lean/Six Sigma Expertise"},{"t